==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed <!-- directly? or via Latin? --> from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|κατάρροος|lang=grc}}, which is derived from {{term|καταρρέω||I flow down|tr=katarréō|lang=grc}}, which is composed of {{term|κατά||down|tr=katá|lang=grc}} and {{term|ῥέω||I flow|tr=rhéō|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kəˈtɑr/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|pathology|lang=en}} [[inflammation|Inflammation]] of the [[mucous membrane]]s of the [[nose]] and [[throat]].
#* {{RQ:Wodehouse Offing|XII|“Where I went wrong,” he said, still speaking in that low, husky voice as if he had been a ghost suffering from '''catarrh''', “was in getting engaged to Phyllis Mills.”}}

